{"entrypoint": "sdk-cli", "isSidechain": false, "message": {"content": [{"text": "The main checkout at `~/broomva` is now on `main`, level with origin/main (0 ahead, 0 behind). The hook that actually fires now passes 9/9 on #777's dogfood, up from 5/9. No one's work was lost.\n\n**Before and after**\n\n| | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Branch | `fix/gates-that-cannot-fail` (7 ahead, 86 behind) | `main` at `3e171a81b` (0 ahead, 0 behind) |\n| Modified tracked files | 6 | 4: the 2 regenerated indexes, plus `paseo-vps-host.md` and `computer-programming.md` carried over untouched |\n| Untracked files | 147 | 147 (not touched) |\n| Registered-hook dogfood | 5/9 | **9/9** |\n| `make bstack-check` | not run | exit 0, hooks section 15 passed, 0 failed |\n\n**Where things are**\n- **Patch** of the 6 modified files: `~/.config/broomva/fleet/main-checkout-20260927T140456.patch`, with the untracked list next to it (`.untracked.txt`).\n- **Rescue branch**: `rescue/main-checkout-20260927T140456` at `493e046cc`, pushed to origin.\n\n**What I found**\n- **The 7 local commits are all on main.** They touched only `Makefile` and `gate-that-cannot-fail.md`, and both files are identical to the #702 squash (`58ddd3795`). The merge commit's other parent is also on main. No rescue was needed for this branch.\n- **The two entity edits are already on main**, every added line, via #732. No PR needed. `Conversations.md` and `knowledge-index.md` were reset to main's copies and then regenerated (`bookkeeping index` produced 1286 entities; `make conversations` ran 9 succeeded, 0 failed).\n- **Something you didn't expect:** the local `main` branch itself had 3 commits that weren't on origin/main (knowledge-graph entities from moltbook runs 338\u2013339). Almost all of it is on main already. The one exception is a body paragraph in `corpus-is-downstream-of-its-own-audit.md` (\"Re-measured four days later\u2026\"). Its facts are on main in lines 10\u201312 (31.6%, @opung's 83%, the role-mix reading, the cutover hazard), but that prose exists only on the rescue branch. That's why I pushed it. I think it's too redundant to be worth a PR, but it's there if you want it.\n\n**Where I departed from your steps**\n- I restored only the 4 files that also changed on main. The other two (`paseo-vps-host.md`, `computer-programming.md`) are unchanged upstream, so they carried across the switch and are still in the working tree rather than only in the patch.\n- One untracked file blocked the switch: `research/entities/pattern/nested-watchdog-inherits-the-skip.md`. It was byte-identical to main's copy. I backed it up to `\u2026/main-checkout-20260927T140456.untracked-backup/` and removed it, and main's identical copy replaced it.\n- The final move was `git checkout -B main origin/main`, not a fast-forward, because local `main` had diverged. I only did it after the rescue branch was pushed.\n\n**Dogfood.** The 5 must-block commands were: the incident command `cd ~ && rm -rf <name>`, the workspace via `cd` plus a relative path, bare `~`, `$HOME/broomva`, and `~/*`. The 4 must-allow controls were `/tmp` cleanup, a filtered glob, a `2>&1` redirect, and `git status`. BRO-2609 describes the cases but doesn't give every literal string, so I rebuilt them from #777's post-merge comment. The script is at `~/.config/broomva/fleet/main-checkout-20260927T140456.dogfood.sh`. I didn't re-run the old hook to reproduce the 5/9 baseline; that figure is from #777. The live gate also blocked my first inline attempt, which contained those strings, so the shield is clearly active.\n\nThe 4 modified files are uncommitted, as they were before: the two regenerated indexes plus the two carried-over edits.\n\nARC-STATUS: CLOSED", "type": "text"}], "role": "assistant"}, "type": "assistant", "uuid": "e6b639a5-a5ea-48a0-8a7e-247a238a3dba"}
